.TH AD_LAYER_LINE_DELETE_IN_PLACE 1 "2026-08-31" "ad 2.0" "ad layers"
.SH NAME
ad_layer_line_delete_in_place \- delete whole lines on their own line (not joined then deleted)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_layer_line_delete_in_place
< post_ops > line_delete_ops
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_layer_line_delete_in_place
detects the pattern: \\n delete on line N, followed by content deletes on line N+1, followed by \\n delete on line N+1. It reorders so content is deleted FIRST (on its own line), then the \\n delete joins. This prevents the "join then delete" visual where two lines briefly merge before the second one vanishes.
.PP
Algorithm:
.PP
.RS
.nf
walk ops:
  if op[i] is delete(\\n) on line N
     and op[i+1..k] is delete(content) on line N+1
     and op[k+1] is delete(\\n) on line N+1:

       emit op[i+1..k]      (content deletes, keep line=N+1)
       emit op[k+1]         (content's \\n, keep line=N+1)
       decrement line of all LATER ops by 1
       op[i] is still delete \\n, re-iterate
  else:
       emit op[i] unchanged
.fi
.RE
.PP
The joiner \\n stays in place. After emitting the content and content's \\n, those ops are removed from the work array and all later ops have their line decremented by 1. Then we re-iterate from the same position \(em op[i] is still the joiner \\n, but now op[i+1] is whatever came after the deleted content. If that forms another match, we process it too.
.SH PIPELINE PLACEMENT
This layer runs on the RAW compute output (before
.BR ad_layer_reorder ),
because it needs the original line numbers from the diff. When
.B \-\-line\-delete\-in\-place
is enabled, it runs INSTEAD of
.BR ad_layer_reorder .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug logging to /tmp/ad_debug/.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
V2 TSV format. Input should be raw compute output (not post-reorder).
.SH CONFIGURATION
No environment variables. This layer has no user-configurable options.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ad_layer_line_delete_in_place < raw_ops.txt > line_delete_ops.txt
Reorder line-delete patterns.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad_postprocess (1),
.BR ad_layer_reorder (1)
.PP
.I docs/src/plugin-layers.md
.PP
